<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What's a good client retention rate for a Dubai salon?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There's no single universal benchmark since it varies by service type, but salons with an active rebooking habit and loyalty system commonly see well over half of clients return within 6-8 weeks, compared to well under that without any system in place."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a loyalty app worth the cost for a small salon?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not always — a simple punch card or a well-tracked spreadsheet with consistent WhatsApp follow-up often outperforms an underused app. The system matters more than the software."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I win back a client without sounding like I'm just chasing a sale?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Lead with genuine interest rather than a discount — asking how their last service is holding up reads as personal rather than transactional."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should rebooking prompts happen at checkout or afterward by message?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Both, ideally — asking in person at checkout catches the moment while the client is happiest, and a WhatsApp follow-up catches anyone who wanted to check their schedule first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a referral program count as retention or acquisition?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Both — it rewards an existing client for staying engaged while bringing in a new client at a lower cost than ads."}}]}</script>

			
			
